quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  12,38,"Instead, I follow the faith of my fathers, Ibrahim (Abraham), Ishaq (Isaac) and Ya‘qub (Jacob). And it is not for us to ascribe any partners to Allah. That is by Allah’s grace upon us and upon all humankind, but most people do not give thanks."
  12,39,"O my fellow prisoners! (Tell me:) Are different gods better, or Allah, the One, the Supreme?"
  12,40,All those (whom) you worship besides Him are only names you and your fathers have coined; Allah has not sent down any authority for them. Authority belongs to Allah alone. He has commanded that you shall worship none but Him. That is the right religion. But most people do not know.
  12,41,"O my fellow prisoners! As for one of you, he will serve wine to his master (i.e. the king of Egypt). As for the other, he will be crucified, and the birds will eat from his head. The matter about which you inquired has been (already) decided.’"
  12,42,"He told the one he thought would be released from among the two: ‘Mention me to your master.’ But Satan made him forget to mention him to his master. So, he remained in prison for several years."
  12,43,"And (one day) the king said: ‘I saw (in a dream) seven fat cows, and that seven skinny ones were eating them. Moreover, (I saw) seven green ears (of corn) and (seven) others (that were) dry. O chiefs (of my council)! Give me your opinion on my dream if you can interpret dreams.’"
